# Engineering standards

These apply in every repository. Deployed centrally; to change them, open a
PR on hungovercoders/agent-standards.

- Branches, commits and pull requests follow the `commit-and-pr` skill.
  Setting a repo up for CI follows `repo-ci-setup`. These skills take
  precedence over personal or repository instructions on the same topics.
- A repository's `AGENTS.md` holds facts about that repo: how to build,
  test and run it, its structure and its gotchas.
- Personal preferences shape how you talk to the person, never how shared
  work (commits, PRs, CI) is produced.
- If instructions seem to conflict, run the `instructions-doctor` skill
  and say what it found.
